   "title": "Fetching a chapter",
   "body": "SuperBook doesn't store any scripture. Each chapter is **loaded when you open it**, from free public APIs, using public-domain translations. The Bible comes from [bible-api.com](https://bible-api.com), in the World English Bible:\n\n```text\nhttps://bible-api.com/Genesis%201?translation=web\n→ { \"verses\": [ { \"verse\": 1, \"text\": \"In the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth.\\n\" }, … ] }\n```\n\n**`async` and `await`.** `fetch()` returns a *promise*: a value that arrives later. Inside an `async` function, `await` pauses that function until the value arrives, without freezing the page, so the code reads top to bottom like ordinary code.\n\n**Errors are normal on the web.** A request can fail (no connection) or come back with an error status. `fetch` only throws for the first kind, so `fetchJson()` checks `res.ok` and throws a readable message itself, with a special one for **429 Too Many Requests**, which free APIs send when you click too fast. `goTo()` wraps everything in `try … catch` and shows the message in the reader instead of breaking.\n\n**The reader may move on.** Click Next three times quickly and three requests are in flight. If the first one is slow, it could arrive *last* and overwrite the chapter you're actually on. So before drawing, `goTo()` checks the chapter it loaded is still the current one:\n\n```js\nif (id !== `${current.key}|${current.section}|${current.chapter}`) return;   // the reader moved on while this loaded\n```\n\nEach verse is shown with its number in a `<sup>`, and its text goes through `esc()`: it comes from someone else's server, so it's never put into the page as HTML.\n\n### Try it\n\nOpen the Bible and page through. (The Tanakh and the Qur'an come in the next step.)",
   "checks": [
    {
     "pane": "js",
     "label": "one function for every request",
     "test": "/async\\s+function\\s+fetchJson\\s*\\(/"
    },
    {
     "pane": "js",
     "label": "a readable error for \"too many requests\"",
     "test": "/res\\.status\\s*===\\s*429/"
    },
    {
     "pane": "js",
     "label": "the Bible from bible-api.com",
     "test": "/bible-api\\.com/"
    },
    {
     "pane": "js",
     "label": "ignore a chapter the reader has left",
     "test": "/if\\s*\\(\\s*id\\s*!==\\s*`/"
    }
   ],
